    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a3">

                <pb facs="0324" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg250"/>

                <head>Telegram sent to Hon.
                        William McDougall</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Toronto,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 13, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William McDougall</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Provincial Secretary, Ottawa, C. W.:</hi></p>
                <p>Is there any reason why Ellis, Dillon, and Carney should not be discharged at
                    once? The evidence of their innocence is certainly conclusive, and has been
                    before your government for a week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. THURSTON, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
